  "scope": [
    "Exploratory three-fleet pilot, nine existing vehicle realizations per fleet; no control runs.",
    "Each family has one vehicle at each training speed. Family labels/true parameters are evaluation-only; opaque IDs and randomized order enter learning.",
    "Exactly one 12 s broadband record per vehicle; full duration is retained. Common zero-state initialization and yaw-only nonlinear OE.",
    "All methods use the same fixed parameter bounds and no previous identified coefficients.",
    "All six local parameters are free. Sharing and grouping omit mu (weight zero); global common-model baseline estimates one shared mu.",
    "Regularization is sum normalized squared yaw residuals plus weighted squared log-parameter deviation. Log prior scales .1 for CT ratios, .25 for lengths are fixed engineering choices, not estimated from test vehicles.",
    "Constant relaxation lengths .4/.7 m are shared across this simulated population, as in the preceding pilot; this is a favorable transfer assumption, not evidence for different tires.",
    "K=3 is a fixed pilot choice. Two training-only initialization attempts; no family labels, test-based K selection or test-based lambda selection.",
    "FedPersonal and FedGroups use exact nonlinear local proximal solves and alternating parameter/center/assignment updates. This is a single-machine emulation of data-local messages, not a network deployment or privacy guarantee.",
    "Global uses summed local Gauss-Newton information and scalar loss messages, with common physical parameters.",
    "Finite budget-exhausted federation models remain visible with explicit convergence flags; no silent fallback. Local OE requires a converged multistart solution.",
    "Evaluation uses disjoint frequencies/phases. Peer-observed, fleet-interpolation and fleet-extrapolation regions are reported separately; extrapolation is never assumed to improve."
  ]
